# RFC 8907 Section 10.5.2: "There MUST always be a shared secret set on the
# server for the client requesting the connection", and "TACACS+ clients MUST
# NOT set TAC_PLUS_UNENCRYPTED_FLAG". A client with no key therefore has no
# conformant packet to send, and tacacsBackend.Build refuses such a server.
#
# WHAT THE REFUSAL DOES, measured rather than assumed. It depends on WHEN the
# bundle is built:
#   - at BOOT, both build sites log the failure and set the bundle nil
#     (`cmd/ze/hub/main.go` no-BGP branch, `cmd/ze/hub/infra_setup.go`). A nil
#     bundle denies every authorization (aaa_lifecycle.go). It does NOT deny
#     every login: failover to the local accounts is the documented behavior on
#     every surface (owner ruling, 2026-09-04), because a login is how the
#     operator reaches the box to repair the config.
#   - at RELOAD, `ze config commit` REFUSES and rolls back
#     (`cmd/ze/hub/main_reload.go`, "reload: rebuild aaa bundle"), but only
#     while a bundle is already live: the rebuild is skipped when it is nil.
#
# WHAT THIS TEST PROVES, and what it used to. The daemon STARTS, reads the
# config, drops the tacacs backend from the chain, and keeps running. That is
# the correct behavior, so there is no exit code to assert and none is asserted:
# the evidence is the error text and the backend it names.
#
# It asserted one until 2026-09-06, and that assertion was the whole reason this
# file passed while proving nothing. The measurement recorded here on 2026-09-04
# -- that `ze -` "ends in exit 1 because a config that starts no BGP and no
# plugin has nothing to run" -- was WRONG. The parse suite's runner rewrote the
# bare `-` into the PATH of the stdin file, so the command ran as `ze <path>`, a
# form the CLI does not have. The daemon answered "unknown command: <path>" with
# its usage text and exit 1 before reading one line of config, and
# `expect=exit:code=1` was satisfied by that. Meanwhile the one line that could
# discriminate, `expect=stderr:pattern=`, was a spelling the parse suite's parser
# did not read and dropped in silence. Both halves are fixed in
# `internal/test/runner/parsing.go`; a bare `ze -` now runs as `ze start <file>`.
#
# VALIDATES: a tacacs server declared with no key is refused by name when the
#            AAA bundle is built.
# PREVENTS: the daemon authenticating against a server whose every packet body,
#           the PAP User-Password included, would go out in cleartext under a
#           header whose unencrypted flag is clear.

stdin=ze-conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
system {
	authentication {
		tacacs {
			server 127.0.0.1 {
				port 49
			}
			timeout 2
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

# The daemon does not exit, so the runner stops it at this deadline and then
# checks the assertion against what it wrote. 3s is 15x the 200ms at which the
# error was observed, and a parallel run widens it by ParallelTimeoutHeadroom.
cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze -:stdin=ze-conf:timeout=3s
# The whole proof, and it binds three facts to one log line: the backend that
# was DROPPED is tacacs, the server is the one this config declares, and the
# reason is ErrNoSharedSecret, which nothing but tacacsBackend.Build produces.
# Each fact is load-bearing. Without the backend name a dropped radius or
# ldap backend would satisfy it; without the error text any drop reason would,
# a refused dial included; without the drop message the error could be logged
# by a path that went on to use the server anyway.
expect=stderr:pattern=backend dropped from the chain.*backend=tacacs error="tacacs server 127\.0\.0\.1:49: no shared secret configured for this TACACS\+ server"
